<title>UK: L-Bank sets 500 bln lire-into-euro 2004 bond.</title>
<headline>L-Bank sets 500 bln lire-into-euro 2004 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Caboto and J.P. Morgan.</p>
<p> BORROWER   L-FINANCE NV</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  L-BANK</p>
<p> AMT  + 500 BLN LIRE  COUPON   * 9.00	MATURITY    05.MAR.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.05    PAY DATE   S-0.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    99.425    SPREAD	=</p>
<p> NOTES   * COUPON BECOMES 5.125 PCT ON 05.MAR.99.</p>
<p>	   S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>	   + REDENOMINATES INTO EUROS AFTER EMU</p>
<p>	   FUNGIBLE WITH EXISTING FRENCH FRANC AND MARK BONDS</p>
<p>	   AFTER EMU</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
